---
/**
 * CAREER DEVELOPMENT & STUDENT SUCCESS · ALUMNI INTERACTION — audit §2E.
 *
 * ⚠ THE PAGE IS THE CARDS. The school issues an "OUR ALUMNI" graphic per person
 * carrying the name, the degree, the institution and the employer. Three are
 * published. That is the whole verified record of its alumni programme, and it
 * is a strong one — a district school naming where its leavers work is rarer
 * than a school saying it "maintains strong alumni links".
 *
 * ═══ SOURCE — data/alumni.ts, read off the school's own cards ═══════════════
 *   Sudhanshu Raj Mishra — B.Tech, Bangalore Institute of Technology → GE Aerospace
 *   Aditya Narayan Singh  — B.Tech, Madan Mohan Malaviya Technical University
 *                                                          → Micron Technology
 *   Navneet Ranjan Mishra — MBA, Faculty of Management Studies, Lucknow
 *                           University → ICICI Prudential
 *
 * ⚠ THE CARDS ARE GRAPHICS, NOT PHOTOGRAPHS, so they run through AcPosters and
 * are shown whole. Cropping one removes the degree and the employer, which is
 * everything the card exists to say.
 *
 * ⚠ TWO CLAIMS WERE REMOVED, BOTH FROM THE STUB'S OWN DATA ENTRY.
 *   'Pradeeptam, its alumni event, is recorded under School Activities' — it is
 *     not. data/schoolActivities.ts lists ten activities and Pradeeptam is not
 *     among them, and the word appears nowhere else in this repository. A
 *     citation to a record that does not exist reads as sourcing, which makes it
 *     the most persuasive kind of invention. Same fault as the 'Kaushal
 *     scholarship' removed from Scholarships, and stripped from the data too.
 *   'brings former students back to speak to current ones' — no talks programme,
 *     mentoring scheme or frequency is published.
 * ASSET REQUIREMENT: the school's own account of its alumni programme.
 *
 * Composition: posters (sand, three cards, strict — no stagger, because this is
 * a register) → path (paper, the route a card describes) → close.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import AcPosters from '../../../components/academics/system/AcPosters.astro';
import AcPath from '../../../components/academics/system/AcPath.astro';
import AcClose from '../../../components/academics/system/AcClose.astro';

import banner from '../../../assets/corridor and stairs/DSC_1221 copy.jpg';
import { getAcademicTopic } from '../../../lib/cms';

const ac = await getAcademicTopic('/academics/student-success/alumni-interaction/');
const gSudhanshu = ac.pic('gSudhanshu');
const gAditya = ac.pic('gAditya');
const gNavneet = ac.pic('gNavneet');
const pCohort = ac.pic('pCohort');

const school = 'Sunbeam School Ballia';
---

<BaseLayout
>
  <PageHero
    src={banner}
  />

  <div class="u-page-panel ac-panel">
    <AcPosters
      ground="sand"
      aspect="4 / 5"
      stagger={false}
      kicker="Our alumni"
      heading="Where they<br /><em>actually ended up</em>"
      body={[
        'Almost every school says it keeps in touch with its leavers. Very few name one. Sunbeam issues a card per alumnus carrying four things — the name, the degree, the institution and the employer — and a reader can check every one of them.',
        'They are printed here as the school made them: whole, uncropped, three of three.',
      ]}
      posters={[
        {
          art: gSudhanshu,
          alt: `${school}’s alumni card for Sudhanshu Raj Mishra — B.Tech, Bangalore Institute of Technology, placed at GE Aerospace`,
          title: 'Sudhanshu Raj Mishra',
          meta: 'GE Aerospace',
          note: 'B.Tech · Bangalore Institute of Technology.',
        },
        {
          art: gAditya,
          alt: `${school}’s alumni card for Aditya Narayan Singh — B.Tech, Madan Mohan Malaviya Technical University, placed at Micron Technology`,
          title: 'Aditya Narayan Singh',
          meta: 'Micron Technology',
          note: 'B.Tech · Madan Mohan Malaviya Technical University.',
        },
        {
          art: gNavneet,
          alt: `${school}’s alumni card for Navneet Ranjan Mishra — MBA, Faculty of Management Studies, Lucknow University, placed at ICICI Prudential`,
          title: 'Navneet Ranjan Mishra',
          meta: 'ICICI Prudential',
          note: 'MBA · Faculty of Management Studies, Lucknow University.',
        },
      ]}
    />

    <AcPath
      ground="paper"
      kicker="What a card claims"
      heading="A card is<br /><em>four steps long</em>"
      body={[
        'Read across rather than down, the three cards describe one route — the same four steps every time, and each of the four checkable by somebody who has never met the school. That is the whole of the claim, and the school makes no other about its alumni: no talks programme, no mentoring scheme, no frequency.',
      ]}
      beats={[
        { k: 'Class XII', body: 'A leaver of Sunbeam Ballia.' },
        { k: 'The degree', body: 'B.Tech, or an MBA — the qualification named on the card.' },
        { k: 'The institution', body: 'Bangalore Institute of Technology, MMMUT, FMS Lucknow.' },
        { k: 'The employer', body: 'GE Aerospace, Micron Technology, ICICI Prudential.' },
      ]}
    />

    <AcClose
      owed={true}
      statement="Named, and<br /><em>still checkable.</em>"
      body="The school publishes three alumni cards, each checkable line by line. It does not publish an alumni event, a talks programme, a mentoring scheme or how a former student registers — so none is described here."
      photo={pCohort}
      alt={`Student council office-bearers and NCC cadets of ${school} on stage with the school’s dignitaries`}
      position="50% 38%"
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  div.ac-panel { padding-block: 0; }
</style>
